My first ascended character was a wizard, and I think I'd recommend
that others try the same. I reckon it's a bit more interesting than a
valk, because there are lots of different things you can do =96 and if
it comes down to it then you can just fight every battle by carving
elbereth with your magic-bane (I reckon magic-bane is one of the great
advantages of a wizard).

Anyway, if you want to get your first ascension, I recommend that you
stick to just a couple of classes rather than trying them all. Focus
on one class, but try others just to keep the game interesting and to
remind yourself of the strengths and weaknesses of each class.

If you aren't necessary looking to ascend, but rather to just do
reasonably well, then I suggest that the monk is a pretty easy class
to play. When I was new, I found the monk to be by far the easiest,
and great fun. You start with a bunch of food; you don't have to worry
as much about how to get various resistances or how to get good
weapons; you get a reasonable shot at casting spells and hand-to-hand
combat. But I don't think monk's are easy to ascend. I just think they
are a bit less likely to die in the early game.


